# Battle State Persistence System

## Core State Elements [to-do]
- Identify essential battle state that requires persistence
- Implement serializable state structure
- Define minimal required state for battle recovery
- Create simple versioning system for state format

## Basic Persistence Strategy [to-do]
- Save complete state at battle phase transitions
- Implement manual save points for critical events
- Create simple local backup before server transmission
- Store only delta changes during active combat

## Client-Server Communication [to-do]
- Implement basic state synchronization protocol
- Define server authority over critical state elements
- Create simple conflict resolution for state divergence
- Design reconnection flow for interrupted sessions

## Error Recovery [to-do]
- Implement basic error detection for failed saves
- Create fallback to last known good state
- Design simple retry mechanism for persistence failures
- Log critical errors for debugging

The MVP implementation should prioritize reliability over complexity. Start with core functionality that ensures battles can be saved and resumed, then iterate with more advanced features as needed. 